#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1349 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "FRESH. A 2-vs-1 split: STUDY-A is the unique most-common value, so only the minority row (STUDY-B) is flagged -- the boundary the 1-vs-1 twin fixtures cannot show, since a tie flags every non-blank row."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 STUDYID=STUDY-B DOMAIN=DM
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SUBJID  type=Char label="Subject Identifier for the Study"
col SEX     type=Char label="Sex"
---
STUDY-A | DM | STUDY-A-001 | 001 | M
STUDY-A | DM | STUDY-A-002 | 002 | F
STUDY-B | DM | STUDY-B-003 | 003 | M
